This research aims at investigating the correlation between taxi trip distance and taxi trip duration within the city of New York. In particular, this research 
will attempt to discover if there is an evident pattern of longer trip distances being correlated with longer trip duration, or if there are external 
influences, such as traffic condition and time of the day that have a larger effect. In this research, the dataset used will be the NYC TLC Yellow Taxi Trip Record 
Data. This data set has trip distance information and the timestamps for pick-up and drop-off. The trip duration will be calculated based on the timestamps, 
so that we can compare the trip duration and trip distance. The set also contains information about the pickup and drop off zones that can be considered in the 
analysis.
